    {
      "id": "windowed-collection-instructions",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Discussion Map",
      "position": {
        "x": -220,
        "y": 700
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "windowed-collection-view"
        },
        "markdown": "# Discussion Map\n\nUse the semantic edges to follow the proposal:\n\n- large collections **motivate** a bounded browsing window\n- authors and visitors are **affected by** crowded collection surfaces\n- the idea **assumes** windowing can remain presentation-only\n- existing list virtualization **informs** the membership question\n- observed virtualization behavior **supports** the presentation assumption\n- explicit page graphs **question** directory discovery\n- address-changing file moves **threaten** the idea\n- a ten-member prototype **tests** the assumption and the proposed surface **advances** the idea\n\nMembership comes from repository structure. Direct `.node` files and `root.node` files in direct child directories become collection members; the collection’s own `root.node` and deeper descendants do not. Scrolling changes browser state, not authored graph state."
      }
    },
