      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Collections Become Visually Unusable Before They Become Conceptually Large",
        "statement": "A collection graph may remain understandable as a set, yet rendering every member simultaneously crowds the canvas and makes browsing increasingly awkward.",
        "impact": "Authors lose a useful collection surface and visitors cannot scan members comfortably, even though the underlying graph and membership model are still adequate.",
        "urgency": "high",
        "definitionKey": "idea-problem",
        "_classBinding": {
